menu "Gateway: commissioning access point"

    config GW_SOFTAP
        bool "Wi-Fi access point for commissioning (NET-5)"
        depends on GW_WIFI
        default y
        help
            Starts a WPA2 access point "GW-Setup-XXXXXX" (last bytes of the MAC) with the
            device's commissioning password when there is no valid configuration (rejected,
            or after a factory reset) and on a 2-10 s press of BOOT. The web UI is then at
            the address of the access point (192.168.4.1, the ESP-IDF default): https with the
            default web.https (plain HTTP only redirects), http with web.https false. The log
            line gives the address in use.
            Needs the Wi-Fi driver (CONFIG_GW_WIFI): QEMU has no radio.

    config GW_SOFTAP_TIMEOUT_MIN
        int "Minutes the access point stays up after a BOOT press (valid configuration)"
        depends on GW_SOFTAP
        range 1 1440
        default 30

endmenu
